WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.494 --> 00:00:02.905
- Sometimes, an indirect route

00:00:02.905 --> 00:00:04.556
is the quickest way to get there.

00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:06.135
Do something that you know you can do

00:00:06.135 --> 00:00:08.291
and go for it at 150 million percent.

00:00:08.291 --> 00:00:11.445
I just wanted to be the best, be hot,

00:00:11.445 --> 00:00:14.483
and just have something hot,
hear my voice on the radio.

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:16.023
You don't have to stop.

00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:17.244
It's just a matter of

00:00:17.244 --> 00:00:18.894
you caring enough to always pay attention.

00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:22.226
I just make my records
and let the chips fall.

00:00:22.226 --> 00:00:23.972
You can do anything you put your mind to,

00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:25.331
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:25.331 --> 00:00:26.164
There's no limitations to this.

00:00:26.164 --> 00:00:28.258
Dad, you're fired.

00:00:28.258 --> 00:00:31.882
You, my assistant, you're fired too.

00:00:31.882 --> 00:00:33.186
You, you're fired.

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:34.516
Everybody's fired.

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:35.421
Be like a tiger.

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:37.311
Just attack your dreams

00:00:37.311 --> 00:00:39.296
with aggression and power.

00:00:39.296 --> 00:00:41.519
If I'm not here to maximize my potential,

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:43.027
then what am I on earth for?

00:00:43.027 --> 00:00:45.997
You're not successful 'til
you've went 360 degrees

00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:48.655
full cipher, the full cycle, then die.

00:00:48.655 --> 00:00:49.975
Then you're successful.

00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:51.812
He's an American hip hop recording artist

00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:53.789
and actor from Queens, New York.

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:56.219
He's known as one of the
forefathers of pop rap.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:58.400
He's released 13 studio albums

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.305
and two greatest hits compilations.

00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:04.472
He's LL Cool J, and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:07.346 --> 00:01:10.170
You know, where I come from,
people are very passionate.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.488
Hot blooded.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.595
They want it.

00:01:12.595 --> 00:01:13.884
They want it now!

00:01:13.884 --> 00:01:16.620
I need it right away! Everyone's
looking for a shortcut,

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.203
but sometimes an indirect route

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.396
is the quickest way to get there.

00:01:22.396 --> 00:01:24.943
Sometimes you've got
to take a little longer

00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:27.386
to achieve the things
you will achieve in life.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:28.999
So don't be in a hurry.

00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:29.916
Be patient.

00:01:31.254 --> 00:01:32.171
Be patient.

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:36.068
Everybody wants everything now.

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:38.476
We live in a society where
there's instant gratification.

00:01:38.476 --> 00:01:40.241
Instagram, insta-this.

00:01:40.241 --> 00:01:41.514
Be patient.

00:01:41.514 --> 00:01:43.338
- [Interviewer] A lot of
kids, when they're growing up,

00:01:43.338 --> 00:01:45.140
there's a lot of stuff they
think that they can't do.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.757
They're told they can't be
this, they can't be that.

00:01:46.757 --> 00:01:48.486
- What you have to do is, if you're

00:01:48.486 --> 00:01:52.545
in a situation like that, you
have to gain focus in yourself

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.807
and go forward yourself.

00:01:54.807 --> 00:01:55.970
Don't listen.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.455
- So how do you--
- Just focus.

00:01:57.455 --> 00:01:58.991
- [Interviewer] How would
you tell somebody to do that

00:01:58.991 --> 00:01:59.824
if they don't have that power,

00:01:59.824 --> 00:02:00.973
they think they're not capable of it?

00:02:00.973 --> 00:02:02.906
- You got to get confidence
and find something

00:02:02.906 --> 00:02:05.061
that you do feel confident about.

00:02:05.061 --> 00:02:07.618
Find something that you feel
confident you can achieve.

00:02:07.618 --> 00:02:09.607
Do something that you know you can do

00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:12.690
and go for it at 150 million percent.

00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:16.116
- [Interviewer] So how
did you know it was music?

00:02:16.116 --> 00:02:17.286
- That's what I like.

00:02:17.286 --> 00:02:18.552
I know.

00:02:18.552 --> 00:02:19.709
It's what I love.

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:20.588
- [Interviewer] For real,
from the first time?

00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:22.054
- Absolutely.
- Way back when?

00:02:22.054 --> 00:02:23.054
- Absolutely.

00:02:23.054 --> 00:02:25.001
For me, it doesn't matter what I do.

00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:26.797
I could do all of the Hollywood stuff

00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:30.122
and I do all that, and
everybody knows about that part

00:02:30.122 --> 00:02:31.171
of my life.

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:32.028
Yeah, all of that.

00:02:32.028 --> 00:02:33.065
But you know what?

00:02:33.065 --> 00:02:35.288
There is nothing on earth

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.538
more fun and crazy and wild

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.009
for me than just getting
on the records and rhyming

00:02:41.009 --> 00:02:45.439
and hear my joint on the
radio, hear my joint at a club.

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:48.136
Yo, look, I could host a zillion Grammys.

00:02:48.136 --> 00:02:52.052
I could do TV shows or shoot
bazookas and blow cars up

00:02:52.052 --> 00:02:55.110
and do all of that, but
none of that gives me

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:59.364
the adrenaline rush and the
thrill that music gives me.

00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:01.318
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:01.318 --> 00:03:02.960
And so when you put your heart

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.903
and soul and your passion
into something, I can't walk

00:03:04.903 --> 00:03:08.752
away from that just because
it never was business for me.

00:03:08.752 --> 00:03:10.135
It was always personal.

00:03:10.135 --> 00:03:11.976
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:13.113
Music was always personal

00:03:13.113 --> 00:03:15.180
to me and I know that's almost
weird and that everywhere

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.429
it's all about being a
businessman, but for me,

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:19.354
music was always personal.

00:03:19.354 --> 00:03:21.024
I just wanted to be the best,

00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:23.514
be hot, and just have something hot,

00:03:23.514 --> 00:03:27.174
hear my voice on the radio,
be heard, and just feel it.

00:03:27.174 --> 00:03:29.062
That's what my whole career
is based on, you know.

00:03:29.062 --> 00:03:31.850
Longevity, versatility, originality,

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.364
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:33.364 --> 00:03:35.608
Giving them the longevity,

00:03:35.608 --> 00:03:37.594
but being versatile enough
to adapt as time moves on.

00:03:37.594 --> 00:03:40.774
And then being original
enough, not being a follower,

00:03:40.774 --> 00:03:44.106
not being a guy that, you
know, you're leading the pack

00:03:44.106 --> 00:03:45.965
and then when things
switch up, all the sudden

00:03:45.965 --> 00:03:47.309
you start following.

00:03:47.309 --> 00:03:49.298
But actually keeping it fresh,

00:03:49.298 --> 00:03:52.377
still believing in your taste.

00:03:52.377 --> 00:03:53.464
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:53.464 --> 00:03:56.826
I got a lot of little young
homies that stay around me

00:03:56.826 --> 00:04:00.143
and a lot of little cats
that I hang out with

00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:03.646
and stuff like that, but
just believing in yourself

00:04:03.646 --> 00:04:05.244
and doing what you love.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.554
That's the thing I love

00:04:06.554 --> 00:04:07.437
about this culture.

00:04:07.437 --> 00:04:09.014
You don't have to stop.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:10.549
It's just a matter of you caring enough

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:11.850
to always pay attention.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.241
- To what's going on?

00:04:13.241 --> 00:04:14.315
- Absolutely.

00:04:14.315 --> 00:04:18.482
Well, see, with me, I don't
concentrate on black or pop.

00:04:20.205 --> 00:04:22.484
I make an LL record, I make
the best record I can make,

00:04:22.484 --> 00:04:25.800
I put it out there and
present it to the people.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:26.633
You know?

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:30.991
I mean, it's like a painting.

00:04:30.991 --> 00:04:34.783
I mean, if 500 people get
online to see my painting today

00:04:34.783 --> 00:04:36.922
the next painting is 5,000,

00:04:36.922 --> 00:04:38.677
and the next painting is 3,000,

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.422
and the next painting is 40,000

00:04:40.422 --> 00:04:43.632
and the next painting is 2,000

00:04:43.632 --> 00:04:45.165
that's just the way it is.

00:04:45.165 --> 00:04:48.415
You know, I'm interested in radio play,

00:04:50.969 --> 00:04:53.385
but at the same time, I
just make what I make,

00:04:53.385 --> 00:04:56.013
and I don't know how to cross over.

00:04:56.013 --> 00:04:59.064
I don't know how to go pop.

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:02.425
I just make my records
and let the chips fall.

00:05:02.425 --> 00:05:05.396
I got a line on the album, I
don't remember the exact line,

00:05:05.396 --> 00:05:07.121
but I was just basically saying that

00:05:07.121 --> 00:05:09.611
when my first album dropped,
Jordan was a rookie.

00:05:09.611 --> 00:05:11.197
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:11.197 --> 00:05:12.239
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:05:12.239 --> 00:05:14.244
- You know what I'm saying,
just to put it in perspective,

00:05:14.244 --> 00:05:17.072
my first album cover, I had
the first ever pair of Jordans

00:05:17.072 --> 00:05:19.460
from the first release.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.293
The first--

00:05:20.293 --> 00:05:22.224
- [Radio Host] Is that
standing on the car?

00:05:22.224 --> 00:05:24.048
- Yeah, no, no, that's my second album.

00:05:24.048 --> 00:05:27.350
This is my first one,
and you know, it's crazy,

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.826
because it just shows you
that you can do anything

00:05:30.826 --> 00:05:32.309
you put your mind to,
you know what I'm saying,

00:05:32.309 --> 00:05:33.882
there's no limitations to this.

00:05:33.882 --> 00:05:36.531
There was a point when I started hearing,

00:05:36.531 --> 00:05:38.879
"You know, you're having tax problems."

00:05:38.879 --> 00:05:42.643
But my father was running
my whole financial life.

00:05:42.643 --> 00:05:44.534
He was dealing with the checks,

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:45.389
he was dealing with everything.

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:46.932
I hardly was doing anything,

00:05:46.932 --> 00:05:48.682
and around that time,

00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:53.811
I was starting to get back
with the mother of my children.

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:55.820
And I remember looking at
my son and saying to myself,

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:59.737
you know, how can I look
at this young man here

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.770
and tell him I'm his father

00:06:06.422 --> 00:06:09.589
if I'm not even taking care of myself?

00:06:12.283 --> 00:06:14.876
I have all these people around
me telling me what to do

00:06:14.876 --> 00:06:16.459
and what not to do.

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:21.351
Who I should be with, and
who I shouldn't be with.

00:06:21.351 --> 00:06:23.177
And I have a son here
who's going to depend on me

00:06:23.177 --> 00:06:27.715
to take care of him and
look out for him, raise him.

00:06:27.715 --> 00:06:29.215
Dad, you're fired.

00:06:30.487 --> 00:06:33.573
You, my assistant, you're fired too.

00:06:33.573 --> 00:06:34.956
You, you're fired.

00:06:34.956 --> 00:06:36.569
Everybody's fired.

00:06:36.569 --> 00:06:37.984
Yeah, hello?

00:06:37.984 --> 00:06:39.635
Yeah, I'm trying to figure out

00:06:39.635 --> 00:06:40.978
where the GD program is.

00:06:40.978 --> 00:06:42.154
Oh, I know where it is.

00:06:42.154 --> 00:06:45.220
My uncle tells me, I go out there.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:46.053
I join in.

00:06:46.955 --> 00:06:48.490
You understand what I'm saying?

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.298
It's like there's a period, you know,

00:06:50.298 --> 00:06:52.370
you got to take control,
you got to take the reins.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.456
Yes, I have people in
my life that help me,

00:06:54.456 --> 00:06:58.211
because you know, wise men
attains wise counsel, obviously.

00:06:58.211 --> 00:07:00.590
And you want to have that
mastermind principle going on.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.589
You want to have a lot
of people around you,

00:07:02.589 --> 00:07:04.187
have a think tank flowing.

00:07:04.187 --> 00:07:05.937
But at the same time,

00:07:06.902 --> 00:07:09.033
you got to be able to take
care of your own life,

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:10.498
and that was what was important to me.

00:07:10.498 --> 00:07:12.379
I decided, you know
what, I want to be able

00:07:12.379 --> 00:07:14.043
to take care of my own life.

00:07:14.043 --> 00:07:15.593
I have to be able

00:07:15.593 --> 00:07:18.267
to be in charge, on some
level, of my own life.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:21.933
I guess what it all boils
down to at the end of the day

00:07:21.933 --> 00:07:25.572
is how bad you want it,
how hard are you willing

00:07:25.572 --> 00:07:27.903
to work for it and what are you willing

00:07:27.903 --> 00:07:30.000
to sacrifice to get it?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.583
You don't have to
sacrifice your integrity.

00:07:34.599 --> 00:07:37.747
You don't have to sacrifice
who you are as a human being,

00:07:37.747 --> 00:07:39.748
the principles, the values
that are instilled in you

00:07:39.748 --> 00:07:43.018
by your mentors or your family.

00:07:43.018 --> 00:07:45.335
You may have to sacrifice some sleep.

00:07:45.335 --> 00:07:49.169
The successful people in this
room lost a lot of sleep.

00:07:49.169 --> 00:07:50.018
Oh, yeah.

00:07:50.018 --> 00:07:51.385
They're tired now; look at them.

00:07:51.385 --> 00:07:54.425
Bags under their eyes; "Oh,
God, when's he going to finish?

00:07:54.425 --> 00:07:55.703
"Jesus.

00:07:55.703 --> 00:07:56.703
"Oh, my God.

00:07:58.256 --> 00:08:00.506
"I love the kids, but God."

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.453
Which, you know,

00:08:07.777 --> 00:08:09.592
that's really what it's about.

00:08:09.592 --> 00:08:11.378
Just believing in yourself.

00:08:11.378 --> 00:08:13.545
So I say that to say this:

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:19.359
Keep going after your dreams,
keep going after your goals,

00:08:19.359 --> 00:08:20.916
pursue them relentlessly.

00:08:20.916 --> 00:08:23.012
Dig deep down into your soul.

00:08:23.012 --> 00:08:25.317
Hold onto that dream that's inside of you.

00:08:25.317 --> 00:08:26.614
Don't let go no matter what.

00:08:26.614 --> 00:08:27.969
Be like a pit bull.

00:08:27.969 --> 00:08:29.385
Be like a tiger.

00:08:29.385 --> 00:08:32.095
Just attack your dreams with aggression

00:08:32.095 --> 00:08:36.417
and power, but be polite
while you're doing it.

00:08:36.417 --> 00:08:38.987
Have faith in yourself.

00:08:38.987 --> 00:08:41.147
Have faith in your god.

00:08:41.147 --> 00:08:44.457
Listen to your mentors, and love you.

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:46.311
You know, my mother used to
tell me, "Todd, you can do

00:08:46.311 --> 00:08:48.011
"anything you put your mind to."

00:08:48.011 --> 00:08:50.500
And my grandmother used
to tell me, "If a task

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.909
"is once begun, never
leave it til it's done.

00:08:52.909 --> 00:08:56.009
"be thy labor great or small,
do it well or not at all."

00:08:56.009 --> 00:08:58.181
And I kind of grew up with that mantra.

00:08:58.181 --> 00:09:00.543
I grew up believing that you can do

00:09:00.543 --> 00:09:02.848
anything you put your mind to.

00:09:02.848 --> 00:09:03.848
And I don't,

00:09:06.292 --> 00:09:09.792
no matter what, I am extremely determined.

00:09:11.753 --> 00:09:12.706
I am abnormally--

00:09:12.706 --> 00:09:16.167
- That need to succeed
never goes away, right?

00:09:16.167 --> 00:09:18.250
- It's not just a general

00:09:21.552 --> 00:09:24.432
succeed for the sake of succeeding.

00:09:24.432 --> 00:09:28.693
It's a desire to create,
you know what I'm saying?

00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:32.433
To use the godly power and
talent that was instilled in me

00:09:32.433 --> 00:09:35.912
to the best of my ability,
to maximize my potential.

00:09:35.912 --> 00:09:38.512
Because if I'm not here
to maximize my potential,

00:09:38.512 --> 00:09:40.638
then what am I on earth for?

00:09:40.638 --> 00:09:43.303
- [Interviewer] How do you
set goals for yourself?

00:09:43.303 --> 00:09:45.399
- Decide what you want to do and do it.

00:09:45.399 --> 00:09:47.473
- [Interviewer] Do they
change all the time?

00:09:47.473 --> 00:09:48.907
- The quicker you set your goals,

00:09:48.907 --> 00:09:50.103
the quicker you'll achieve them.

00:09:50.103 --> 00:09:52.027
As you achieve them, they change.

00:09:52.027 --> 00:09:53.697
- [Interviewer] So what would
make you, when you go to bed

00:09:53.697 --> 00:09:56.231
at night, what makes you
think yeah, I'm successful?

00:09:56.231 --> 00:09:57.806
- I don't.
- You don't?

00:09:57.806 --> 00:09:59.445
- I don't feel like I'm successful.

00:09:59.445 --> 00:10:01.011
Success, to me,

00:10:01.011 --> 00:10:03.178
is living a complete life,

00:10:04.301 --> 00:10:07.805
being rich physically,
mentally, and spiritually,

00:10:07.805 --> 00:10:12.444
and dying rich physically,
mentally, and spiritually,

00:10:12.444 --> 00:10:15.118
and then ascending to a higher place.

00:10:15.118 --> 00:10:16.610
That's success.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.110
Because you could say you're successful

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:22.277
and then next day lose what you
thought made you successful.

00:10:23.445 --> 00:10:27.467
So you're not successful
til you went 360 degrees

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:30.032
full cipher, the full cycle, and die.

00:10:30.032 --> 00:10:33.312
Then you're successful
because you completed life.

00:10:33.312 --> 00:10:36.504
You were successful with the whole thing.

00:10:36.504 --> 00:10:37.697
- [Interviewer] Where'd you get that?

00:10:37.697 --> 00:10:39.058
- Me.

00:10:39.058 --> 00:10:40.819
- [Interviewer] Yeah?

00:10:40.819 --> 00:10:41.997
Is that something that came

00:10:41.997 --> 00:10:43.812
from your mom or your parents or?

00:10:43.812 --> 00:10:44.645
- Mm-mm.
- Really?

00:10:44.645 --> 00:10:48.382
Because it does ascribe to
some certain religious ideas.

00:10:48.382 --> 00:10:51.801
- For me, this is something I feel inside.

00:10:51.801 --> 00:10:53.987
My life force tells me that.

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:55.362
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:55.362 --> 00:10:57.100
- We made this video
because Rodney asked us to.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.655
If you have another entrepreneur
you want us to profile,

00:10:59.655 --> 00:11:01.517
leave it in the comments below.

00:11:01.517 --> 00:11:04.540
- I'd also love to know which
of LL Cool J's top 10 rules

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.932
